# The living specs in docs/ ARE committed: 106 comments across 81 source files cite them by
# section as the normative behaviour, and `pnpm test` checks the wire protocol against
# docs/wire-protocol.md. A spec the repo does not carry cannot be reviewed beside the change
# that alters it, and a fresh clone could not run the suite at all.
#
# What stays out is the parity campaign's records and the audit artifacts. The campaign docs
# (PARITY, UI-FIDELITY, SPACING-REVIEW, MOBILE-*, PLAN-retired, compat-status, capabilities/,
# research/) now live OUTSIDE the repo, at ../kelpi-docs, and are referenced by hand. Only the
# generated audit output still lands under docs/, so only it is ignored here.
docs/audit/
